# Generated benchmark/diagnostic output. tests/test_all.py writes
# reports/{cmd}_{mode}_{timestamp}.txt on every run and creates the directory
# itself, so the files are disposable and the folder need not be tracked.
reports/

# graphify's own generated artifacts. graph.json / graph.html / GRAPH_REPORT.md
# stay tracked — they are the thing the standing "query the graph first"
# instruction reads. These two are not:
#   cache/   AST extraction cache, ~9 MB, rebuilt on demand by `graphify update .`
#   <date>/  rotating backups of superseded graphs, ~2-3 MB each
# Together they were ~20 MB of generated files in git history.
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/

# Staging area for files removed 2026-08-06; delete the folder once reviewed.
_trash_2026-08-06/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak

